.TH man 1 "11 August 2025" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
	mvcd - mv a file then cd to where it is
.SH SYNOPSIS
	mvcd destination
.SH DESCRIPTION
	does mv then puts you there. if you specify a dirname, it moves the file there with its current name and cds to that dir.
.br
	if you give a filename, it moves the file to that name then cds to the directory it's in. basically same as mv but yo uend up where the file ends up
.SH OPTIONS
	mv default options work, so -i to prompt before overwrite, -n to not overwrite, -b to make backups, -u for update, -v for verbose
.SH EXAMPLES
	mvcd *.csv csvs
.br
	mvcd sdifji.py ../../ijsdif/jsissbsbbsb.py
.SH BUGS
	probably none
